# Service Account Keys and Secrets
#
# `*sa*.json` used to head this list and matched ANY filename containing the
# letters "sa" — it silently swallowed fixtures/work_passages.json ("pas-SA-ges"),
# which passed locally and failed only in CI, where the file had never been
# committed. A secret filter that quietly excludes ordinary files trains people
# to use `git add -f`, which is how a real key eventually gets committed. These
# patterns target credential filenames specifically; `scripts/deploy_gcp.sh`
# never writes key files, and the runtime uses ambient identity, not key JSON.
*-sa.json
*_sa.json
sa-*.json
sa_*.json
*service-account*.json
*serviceaccount*.json
*-credentials.json
*_credentials.json
*private-key*.json
*privatekey*.json
*.pem
*.crt
*.p12
.env
.env.local

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# IDE & OS
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
Hodi-frontend designs/
.hodi_domain_service_urls.json
